---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProviderCard from "../components/ProviderCard.astro";

const providers = [
  { name: "OpenAI", auth: "Bearer key", text: true, image: false },
  { name: "Mistral", auth: "Bearer key", text: true, image: false },
  { name: "Gemini", auth: "Bearer key", text: true, image: true },
  {
    name: "HuggingFace",
    auth: "Bearer key",
    text: true,
    image: false,
    grammar: "model is part of the URL path, not the body",
  },
  {
    name: "Bedrock",
    auth: "Bearer key (AWS bearer API key)",
    text: true,
    image: false,
    grammar: "[<region>/]<modelId>[#<input_type>]",
  },
  {
    name: "Vertex AI",
    auth: "Bearer (GCP OAuth2 token)",
    text: true,
    image: false,
    grammar: "[<location>/<project>/]<modelId>[#<task_type>]",
  },
  {
    name: "Azure",
    auth: "Bearer (Entra token, default) or api-key",
    text: true,
    image: false,
    grammar: "[foundry:]<deployment>[#<input_type>]",
  },
];

const chatProviders = [
  "openai", "mistral", "gemini", "groq", "deepseek",
  "together", "openrouter", "xai", "fireworks",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Providers"
  description="Every provider Zerocache supports: 9 OpenAI-wire chat endpoints, Anthropic /v1/messages, and 7 embedding providers (text + image)."
>
  <h1>Providers</h1>
  <p>
    Every request is bring-your-own-key: Zerocache never holds a provider credential beyond the
    duration of one request. <code>{"{provider}"}</code> in the URL path selects which adapter
    handles the request; the three cloud embedding providers encode routing coordinates (region,
    project, input type) into the <code>model</code> string itself rather than a new wire field,
    since <code>model</code> is already free-form per-request and already lands in the cache key.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Chat completions</h2>
    <p>
      <code>POST /{"{provider}"}/v1/chat/completions</code> — nine hosted OpenAI-wire endpoints,
      registered with zero config. Add or repoint one (self-hosted vLLM / Ollama, an internal
      gateway) with <code>ZEROCACHE_CHAT_PROVIDERS="name=url,…"</code>, where the URL is the prefix
      up to but not including <code>/chat/completions</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="chip-row">
      {chatProviders.map((n) => <code class="chip">{n}</code>)}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Anthropic Messages</h2>
    <p>
      <code>POST /{"{provider}"}/v1/messages</code> — Claude's native wire shape. Built-in
      <code>anthropic</code> &rarr; <code>https://api.anthropic.com</code>; add or repoint with
      <code>ZEROCACHE_MESSAGES_PROVIDERS="name=url,…"</code> (bare-origin values — the adapter
      appends <code>/v1/messages</code>). <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> is rewritten to
      <code>x-api-key</code> upstream.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Embeddings</h2>
    <div class="provider-grid">
      {providers.map((p) => (
        <ProviderCard
          name={p.name}
          auth={p.auth}
          text={p.text}
          image={p.image}
          grammar={p.grammar}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
    <ul class="notes">
      <li><strong>Gemini</strong> is the only provider with image embeddings, and never reports token usage — <code>usage</code> is always zero on its responses.</li>
      <li><strong>Bedrock</strong> authenticates with an Amazon bearer API key — no AWS SigV4. Titan and Cohere sit behind one router.</li>
      <li><strong>Vertex AI</strong> uses a GCP OAuth2 access token, which lives about an hour; since <code>owner_id</code> is a hash of that credential, a Vertex caller's cache namespace rotates when the token does — fine for one long ingestion run, not across days.</li>
      <li><strong>Azure</strong> registers as a provider only once <code>ZEROCACHE_AZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL</code> or <code>ZEROCACHE_AZURE_FOUNDRY_BASE_URL</code> is set; with neither, <code>/azure/v1/embeddings</code> 404s. It covers the Azure OpenAI GA path and Foundry Models.</li>
      <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> and <strong>Mistral</strong> take a configurable base URL, so a self-hosted wire-compatible endpoint (vLLM, LM Studio, TGI) works too. The cloud adapters are mock-tested only — no live-key smoke test in this environment.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .provider-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .chip-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .chip {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: var(--hairline);
    padding: 2px 8px;
  }
  .notes {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 64ch;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .notes li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .notes strong {
    color: var(--paper);
  }
</style>
